            "review_title": "Review at Pho Thin Lo Duc",
            "review_text": "Russ Lacuata\nLong Beach, California9995 contributions\n0\nVery Popular with Locals and Tourists\nSep 2026 • Solo\nPho Thin Lo Duc is located in the French Quarter, a hike away from the Old Quarter. But its so worth it! \nThe atmosphere is locals eating next to tourists from all over. It is communal dining sharing a long table. You pay first when you get in, only one type of Pho 100K for a bowl, 10K for a small quay and 5K for iced tea. The bowl came out steaming hot, you can definitely smell the aroma of the beefy goodness. The broth is clean with a little flavor of fat floating from the beef and of course love the spring onions. Its beefy, hint of some spices, I didnt need to add it to enjoy the soup. But after a few slurps I added lime, some chili peppers, garlic vinegar and chili sauce. That definitely kick it up a notch. The beef is tender and juicy. The noodle texture is on the softer side to my liking. \n\nOverall I was impressed and now I see the hype is real.\nRead more\nWritten September 8, 2026",
